            <ArticleTitle>Bupropion for the treatment of neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1049909110361229</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuropathic pain is a common problem in clinical practice, affecting patients physically, emotionally, financially, and socially. Current treatment includes antidepressants, antiepileptics, and opioid analgesics. Bupropion is a specific inhibitor of neuronal noradrenaline reuptake and a weak inhibitor of dopamine reuptake, which shows some promise in the treatment of neuropathic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
